#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119719 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119971 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91583cc4-29ef-5824-baee-f101cbf49be9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Surface Area of a Sphere Given Its Radius or Diameter"}] :question/id #uuid "fba82316-1ea7-5c90-88d7-37b96172a7f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-9004" :question/problem "A sphere has a diameter of $3 \\: \\textrm{in}$. Find the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac{3}{2} \\: \\textrm{in}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi \\left(\\dfrac {3} {2} \\right)^2 = 9\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119720 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119972 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21358fb6-456e-5ab7-99f4-fc211310df13" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Radius or Diameter of a Sphere Given Its Surface Area"}] :question/id #uuid "e65da51f-3cfc-511a-948c-ba8a46559bba" :question/math-academy-id "e-9005" :question/problem "Calculate the radius of a sphere given that its surface area is $50\\pi \\: \\textrm{cm}^2$.\n\n![](images/99/99bb0ea67859fbd109442fcf698427ea43452087b4523b7202a760a2a8b27052.png)" :question/worked-solution "We can calculate the surface area of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nS = 4 \\pi r^2\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nS=50\\pi \\: \\textrm{cm}^2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n50π &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n\\frac{50π}{4π} &= r^{2} \\\\\nr^{2} &= \\frac{25}{2} \\\\\nr &= \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}cm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119721 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119973 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5161a164-780d-5876-a8e2-458105dc8cab" :knowledge-point/title "Relating the Surface Area and Volume of a Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "acdb3e99-89dd-5463-871e-e4d5d370c827" :question/math-academy-id "e-9008" :question/problem "The volume of the sphere is $\\dfrac{500}{3}\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^3$. Calculate the surface area of the sphere." :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac 4 3 \\pi r^3\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV=\\dfrac{500}{3}\\pi \\: \\textrm{in}^3\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we can solve for $r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n\\frac{500}{3}π &= \\frac{4}{3}πr^{3} \\\\\n\\frac{500π \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 4π} &= r^{3} \\\\\nr^{3} &= 125 \\\\\nr &= 5in\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of ​​the sphere is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS &= 4πr^{2} \\\\\n&= 4π(5)^{2} \\\\\n&= 100πin^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
